We require a highly innovative, dedicated and passionate teacher of design and visual communications (able to teach to NCEA Level 3) to join our well-resourced faculty that includes a recently updated computer suite. Applicants must be NZ registered teachers and familiar with Te Mataiaho.
Karamū High School is a modern campus located in the heart of beautiful, sunny Hawke’s Bay. Our school offers a vibrant and supportive environment where staff thrive professionally and personally.
The successful candidate will show a commitment to:
collaborative teaching and learning;
inspiring ākonga with a desire to learn;
a strong connection with whānau and community;
developing an understanding of mātauranga Māori;
honoring our obligations under Te Tiriti o Waitangi.
All members of our teaching staff are also mentor teachers who support a group of students in their well-being and learning pathway.
Start Term 1 2027.

Located on a picturesque, historic site in Central Auckland, Elim Christian College Mt Albert is a state-integrated Christian school catering for students from Years 0–13. We offer our students a quality education based on Christian values and the New Zealand Curriculum, Te Mātaiaho.
Due to roll growth, we are seeking enthusiastic, dedicated, and highly skilled Year 2–8 kaiako to join our vibrant school community. The successful applicant will thrive in a collaborative environment and be eager to inspire the next generation of learners. Year level (2–8) to be determined based on the candidate's skills, experience, and potential leadership roles.
We also welcome applicants with leadership abilities or aspirations, as there may be opportunities for the right candidate at our school. If you are ready to make a difference, we would love to hear from you!
The successful applicant will:
Be a New Zealand-registered teacher with strong curriculum knowledge;
Uphold the Christian values of our school;
Honour Te Tiriti o Waitangi;
Demonstrate culturally empowering and responsive practices and contexts for teaching and learning;
Establish and maintain strong professional relationships with students, staff, and whānau;
Be a collaborative team player;
Foster a positive classroom environment with high expectations;
Demonstrate a commitment to professional growth and development; and
Be actively involved in the life of the school.
A willingness and ability to participate in religious instruction appropriate to the special character of the school is a condition of appointment.

